  "schema_notes": [
    "Conversations wrapper; ID; Nodes each ID, Text, AllowEscape default true, Choices. Choices Text/Target/Predicates/Actions. Param Key/Value. Predicates conjunctive. Start resolves named Start else first node; End closes; empty or null Target stays and recomputes choices.",
    "No string-token expansion in ConversationLoader. JSON text is literal. C# overlays assemble names, places, current facts and quest states. Keep readable templates rather than pretend one save-specific rendering is canonical.",
    "Source IDs retain legacy names: Marceline=Ondis; BMO=Ellun; RootBeerGuy=Hallun; Crunchy=Belis; Mogu=Solm; Grib=Vurn; Nam=Amai; Sien=Isk; Sopp=Ketch. Use visible names as headings, retain IDs as provenance.",
    "Dialogue is a conditional graph, not one canonical linear playthrough. Export all node/choice branches and gates within a recommended plot order; mark optional/regional alternatives.",
    "HouseDrama definitions contain authoring/backstory and machine-state descriptions; live conversations are HouseVex/HouseThresker JSON. Do not indiscriminately label HouseDrama metadata as spoken dialogue."
  ]
}
